@startuml VickyTruck - Arquitectura Cloud Rediseñada (sin acceso Oracle desde cloud)
title VickyTruck - Arquitectura Cloud Rediseñada (sin acceso Oracle desde cloud)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho

left to right direction

actor "Chofer" as Chofer
actor "Operador Central" as Operador
actor "Operador Local Oracle/APEX" as OperadorLocal

cloud "Cloud (Internet/VPC)" as CLOUD {
  rectangle "Frontend Chofer\n(frontend/)" as FrontChofer {
	component "UI React" as CH_UI
	component "API Client\nservices/api.js" as CH_API
	component "GPS\nservices/geolocation.js" as CH_GPS
	component "Reporte periódico\nservices/ubicacionPeriodica.js" as CH_UBI
	component "Cola offline\nservices/offlineQueue.js" as CH_OFF
  }


  rectangle "Frontend Central\n(central/)" as FrontCentral {
    component "App React Central" as CE_UI
  	component "API Client\nservices/api.js" as CE_API
  	component "Polling\nservices/polling.js" as CE_POLL
	component "MQTT Client\nWebSocket MQTT" as CE_MQTT
  }

  rectangle "Backend API\n(backend/)" as Backend {
    component "REST API Recorridos\n/api/recorridos" as BE_REC
    component "REST API Central\n/api/central" as BE_CEN

    component "Endpoint Integracion Inbound\n/api/integracion/recorridos\n(Alta/actualizacion desde Oracle/APEX local)" as BE_IN_RECORRIDOS
    component "Endpoint Integracion Query\n/api/integracion/estado\n(Consulta arribo/descarga)" as BE_IN_ESTADO

    component "Store Operacional Cloud\n(SQL/NoSQL gestionado)" as BE_STORE
    component "Servicio MQTT Bridge" as BE_MQ_BRIDGE
  }

  queue "Broker MQTT\n(gestionado en cloud)" as MQTT
}

node "Sitio Local (Datacenter/PC)" as LOCAL {
  rectangle "Oracle + APEX" as ORACLE_LOCAL {
    database "Oracle DB" as ORA_DB
    component "APEX / SQLcl / Jobs" as ORA_APEX
  }
}

Chofer --> CH_UI : Usa app de chofer
Operador --> CE_UI : Opera panel 

CH_UI --> CH_API : Lecturas y eventos
CH_API --> CH_GPS : Obtiene lat/lon
CH_UI --> CH_UBI : Inicia reporte periódico
CH_API --> CH_OFF : Encola/reintenta si offline

CE_UI --> CE_API : Consulta/acciones
CE_UI --> CE_POLL : Refresco automático
CE_UI --> CE_MQTT : Suscripcion tiempo real
CE_POLL --> CE_API : GET periódicos

CH_UI --> BE_REC : HTTPS
CE_UI --> BE_CEN : HTTPS

OperadorLocal --> ORA_APEX : Carga/consulta operativa
ORA_APEX --> BE_IN_RECORRIDOS : HTTPS POST/PUT\nPublica recorridos a cloud
ORA_APEX ---> BE_IN_ESTADO : HTTPS GET\nConsulta estado arribos/descargas

BE_IN_RECORRIDOS --> BE_STORE : Upsert recorridos/puntos
BE_IN_ESTADO --> BE_STORE : Lee estados actuales

' Ubicacion en tiempo real por MQTT
CH_UBI --> MQTT : MQTT Publish\nchofer/{fleteId}/ubicacion

CE_POLL --> BE_CEN : Polling para estado/progreso
BE_CEN --> BE_STORE : Lee estado y progreso

CE_MQTT --> MQTT : MQTT Subscribe\nchofer/+/ubicacion

' Backend sigue suscribiendo para persistencia/analytics
MQTT --> BE_MQ_BRIDGE : MQTT Subscribe\nchofer/+/ubicacion
BE_MQ_BRIDGE --> BE_STORE : Persistencia de ubicacion

note left of CLOUD
Cloud NO se conecta a Oracle local.
Toda sincronizacion Oracle/APEX <-> cloud
se hace via endpoints HTTPS del backend.
end note

note top of MQTT
Patron pub/sub:
- Chofer publica ubicacion
- Central consume ubicacion DIRECTO desde MQTT
  (cliente MQTT sobre WebSocket)
end note

legend right
== Flujos clave ==
1. Oracle/APEX local envia recorridos al backend cloud.
2. Oracle/APEX local consulta estado de arribo/descarga al backend cloud.
3. Chofer publica ubicacion en MQTT.
4. Frontend Central se suscribe directo al broker MQTT.
5. Backend consume MQTT en paralelo para persistencia y consultas historicas.
endlegend

@enduml
